        <p> Laos, officially the Lao People's Democratic Republic, is the only landlocked country in Southeast Asia. Known for its mountainous terrain, lush jungles, and the Mekong River, it offers a tranquil, slow-paced alternative to its more developed neighbors. Its culture is deeply rooted in Theravada Buddhism and ancient traditions, and it is famously referred to as the "Land of a Million Elephants".</p>
